    The Markov chain is REVERSIBLE with π ∝ fiber.

========================================================================
  FORCING FIBER FROM BLUE + WIGGLY (n=4)
========================================================================

  Total blue tilings: 0 (expected 2^{m-(n-2)} = 16, match=False)

  CAN WE DERIVE FIBER FROM THE TRANSITION MATRIX?
  The transition matrix P(mi, mj) = W[mi][mj] / (fiber(mi) × m)
  If we know P and W, we can solve: fiber(mi) = W_row_sum(mi) / m

  IS W SYMMETRIC? W[mi][mj] = W[mj][mi]?
  ✓ W IS SYMMETRIC: W[mi][mj] = W[mj][mi] for all pairs

  FIBER DERIVATION:
    Node 0 (H=1, |Aut|=1): W_row=144, fiber=W_row/m=24, actual=24, match=True
